.serverless/

# Server build artifact.
#
# This was tracked in git (2,100+ files) and the Dockerfile ran whatever was
# committed: `COPY server/ .` followed by `CMD ["node", "dist/src/index.js"]`
# with no compile step. The failure mode was silent — pushing correct source
# deployed a stale build and the deploy reported success, which is how a live
# API stayed three weeks behind the repository. The Dockerfile now compiles.
server/dist/

# NOTE: client/dist is still tracked. Firebase Hosting deploys it from disk via
# the firebase CLI (`deploy.sh`), so it does not need to be in git either — but
# untracking it is a separate, larger change and not part of this fix.

